{"title":"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_21\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 21</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">25</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93f84fb27739c43bacdbcd4581f0baeb5290d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\frac{1}{10} + 3\\frac{11}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31bccbbc55b2ccf850fcc2a4aaa068c3aa89467a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5.11 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5.111 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5.12 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5.21 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"467\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc6648300aaed307feda566692a612cbd47e971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)^{10} + (-1)^8 + (-1)^7 + (1)^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"21\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a23cb2a815748149b186c5ec566c64315de6f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 16 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An integer is multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the result is then multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The final result could be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f6e176b1ab306176ae0414852b415732812723b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 64 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 32 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 25 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The greatest number of Mondays that can occur in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive days is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebccb94c356d4c6a364d75aad166d4749fcd39ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/069d711f947f58327434caa042efcfd2d6672c9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 25 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 30 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 55 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Twelve balloons are arranged in a circle as shown. Counting clockwise, every third balloon is popped, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the first one popped. This process continues around the circle until two unpopped balloons remain. The last two remaining balloons are\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/97237c37a697690c6d552dd8ff914021c510aaea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ B, H \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ B, G \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ A, E \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ E, J \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ F, K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"490\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is positive. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c222c89161b10183f69cceae08dfd92f1dbe584a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e94615948b5936bbedbd3dfeb495e5f33d5d7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r, s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> are numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd72b0af2044645af115eb9baca49fdc3fa6a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; s, t &gt; q, q &gt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253bb1bce0adbe169d9013d7cbf3eff483459dad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t &lt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, which of these numbers is greatest?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb9f76193e16fa8ce36773587f6eb47087ca0da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ t \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ s \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ r \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ q \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of seven consecutive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. The smallest of these integers is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da84f38416edd814f5f8dba467fb075912d77b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is assigned, in some order, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689d638ddca59030006d362cbd848607f63aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. The largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048d81618a127ebca7a749afcab86c1da76bf6e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^q + r^s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdda022ae5457a8f45226652194437cdc49b5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 19 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 66 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 82 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 83$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the chart, the products of the numbers represented by the letters in each of the rows and columns are given. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227a15e8ddfdb1ff5d4e66d598c866d83fb40d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db4c731f7825671f6c9f99177b8a5277d875fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are integers, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6b36971f2232e7eb9efe65b0c0b1ad9507de51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xw$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045dcb7a6100daee68be254fa762b2f847d56c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 150 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 300 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 31 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 75 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"415\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three small rectangles, of the same depth, are cut from a rectangular sheet of metal. The area of the remaining piece is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404b48a4ae33b33c0c11ab63a6258b91251111e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$990$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. What is the depth of each cut?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b581e416e9c1955c36601a7c1e5049269c8a3919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is right-angled with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b5b6b078188523fb69a22aff2fbd2b3df42b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bbdd583204bb805c2582d9715858631441d410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 8$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092f4d8a1334b38bf6edbafa359d497739f9017f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 3DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64ad703f83670793144307bb6c70abe64a5c2bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{65} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{80} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{73} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{68}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"448\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be arranged to form twenty-four different four digit numbers. If these twenty-four numbers are then listed from smallest to largest, in what position is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8495fb0c886c0086d9b699f31ee4d9fa62c3c4d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b5ac2c906be8267b032d926afac0ddd2b5efc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13\\text{th} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14\\text{th} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 15\\text{th} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 16\\text{th} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 17\\text{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"475\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88ca2f73a8dc35869c1372f1dc54ff29efdbebe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38ad303643e9161c87ce8c7fbc7af78bce01ca87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> is written as an integer in expanded form. The number of zeros at the end of the resulting integer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85a693778fa54319b2895f4fd33383eee62947a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 70 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 71 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 90 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 140 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"415\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A beam of light shines from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, reflects off a reflector at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and reaches point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdc03b4e24dbee7b5747d6a0aa2def18f5541d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109531931a1b5ca15c856fd22a83cc35da17c0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 32^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 37^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 45^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 26^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 38^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"435\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram adjacent edges are at right angles. The four longer edges are equal in length, and all of the shorter edges are also equal in length. The area of the shape is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f52fdfc136573f67f7b1e38f59b93c08295f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$528$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. What is the perimeter?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/9970336ab91bc8c1e18d87e0eba8f5b29d1151be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 132 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 264 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 92 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 72 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9feeca46d85f71edc9731836fa2e4d4a7a1e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{7} = x + \\frac{1}{y + \\frac{1}{z}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b56d32444d8efd65eb0cb6c01f8ac72c32587e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, then what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc8ba1464f944e344427a3009f6db3f0e272247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad421192cbbf0d038ff69486c1d5cf66cb65609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 11 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 37 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a95da3dc23e00f98c8e373b61bfa0bb453afa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 y z^3 = 7^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793be6cb1ff585c82d60696b6f0ed5f4ecb6c0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^2 = 7^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e7507af346469ed46c7827ad33155703b75e8019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7^2 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7^3 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7^8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7^9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"381\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a circle, fifteen points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8a5b3dff7a5f4cdb3631abafbe26c2afcbbb83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, A_3, \\dots, A_{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> are equally spaced. What is the size of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e5721b87f9769100611a2afbd32159add7c042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 A_3 A_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/17869496c302f60ff520559382cd91c0afb93301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 96^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 100^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 104^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 108^\\circ \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"471\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e9d9818c421f0cfa9f3edec96e6da19b0c2359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left(\\frac{a}{c} + \\frac{a}{b} + 1\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{b}{a} + \\frac{b}{c} + 1\\right)} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, the number of different ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea40f39bec9e50f15db518c930b4305a840ea615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b + c \\leq 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/5335ff32900dc18ab7257c6b67d593b10a87f0ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 33 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 37 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 42 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c319c2d634472426d9f0252c13b3cd98847f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f14bfab0812599d9f00868cbb3ba18c67352b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd95efd6154c9586af431b6dafaf9dd7296ee37f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FBCE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b43db032689b17f3ff1140e06b86c338a9edd22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 144\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 138\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 126\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 108\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 66\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"554\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00bbf02461e1cfd494f409ee97c1861777d7ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34, 55\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />, how many integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> cannot be written as the sum of exactly two elements of the set?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cd8968d639b415069c9ac4a6cbd6a3120aea4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 51 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 57 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 55 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 34 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a convex polygon, exactly five of the interior angles are obtuse. The largest possible number of sides for this polygon is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00ce0a921d15c145d0877e966f9dba6169d92d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a89311289b3da89afb8ef441461963aed309fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BR = RC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c260353f9eb6c0406b15c796d63b13f39b14aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CS = 3SA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/432337f3d55a68793e1a84a7438173d4dcf3707a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AT}{TB} = \\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" />. If the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0418562731679936038fd69468e148b0ff25a698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle RST$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is twice the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e780b0fe7fe62cef3a7645bbe2b9593de4c333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle TBR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" /> is equal to\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd3b778791f7fb75ca2194992091778f4fd51b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{1} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{8}{3} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{7}{4} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"371\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018044045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 648/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 3030/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21261/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   24.049      1 -total\n 29.37%